course: dictionary
lesson: 16055
title: What is viscosity?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Viscosity tells you how thick and sticky a liquid is, and how slowly it flows. Honey has a high viscosity, so it sits in the jar and pours slowly. Water has a low viscosity, so it runs out of a tap quickly.
explain: A liquid with a high viscosity pushes back against flowing. «The honey had a high viscosity, so it dripped slowly off the spoon.» The word tells you why the honey was slow.
explain: Heat usually lowers viscosity. «Warm the honey and it runs much faster.» Warming makes the liquid thinner, so it flows more easily. In science, viscosity is always about how a liquid flows.
fact: Viscosity is a noun for how thick a liquid is and how easily it flows.
fact: A liquid with a high viscosity flows slowly, like treacle.
fact: A liquid with a low viscosity flows quickly, like water.
fact: Heating a liquid usually lowers its viscosity.
fact: Scientists measure viscosity, for example by timing how long a marble takes to fall through a liquid.
exercise: «Honey has a high viscosity.» What does high viscosity mean? | It is always cold | It has no colour | *It flows slowly | It flows very quickly
exercise: Which liquid has a low viscosity? | Syrup | *Water | Treacle | Honey
exercise: Scientists time a marble falling through a liquid. What are they trying to measure? | The weight of the marble | The temperature of the room | *The viscosity of the liquid | The colour of the liquid
test: «Warm the syrup and it pours more easily.» What does heating usually do to viscosity? | Raises it | *Lowers it | Turns it into a gas | Leaves it exactly the same
test: Which liquid would pour most slowly? | Juice | *Treacle | Water | Milk
exam: Which word means how thick and sticky a liquid is, and how slowly it flows? | Density | Volume | Speed | *Viscosity
